  startGame: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 24221b8b4313efa419fd8c0a6a9f28e8, type: 3}
  classDescriptions:
  - 'Fighters devote themselves wholly to all forms of the art of physical combat:
    unarmed fighting, hand-to-hand weapons and missile weapons.'
  - Mages devote themselves to the manipulation of magical forces to achieve their
    ends. Intelligence is the sine qua non of the magic-user, useful for learning
    and casting magic spells, and also for devising original ways to apply a familiar
    spell to a knotty problem.
  - 'Bards travel the land, learning of brave and extraordinary deeds (often committing
    a few themselves along the way) and preserving their memory in song. Not only
    are they learned and quick-tongued, but anyone who travels on foot as much as
    they do should be able to hold their own in a fight, and perhaps hurl a spell
    or two when the need arises. '
  - 'A tinker is skilled at all manner of crafts and mechanical tricks. For survival
    they rely on their thorough knowledge of traps and locks, and their ability to
    repair damaged weapons and armor. '
  - 'Because of their devotion to and understanding of nature, druids are a much-needed
    profession after Britannia''s time of environmental devastation. Most druids
    do not go heavily armored, and rely instead on their mastery of spell-casting
    and woodcraft to evade combat, or utilize their surroundings to their own tactical
    advantage. '
  - Paladins are a specialized group of fighters, devoted to physical fighting on
    behalf of the cause of virtue. The ideological basis of their combat training
    lends them a heroic charisma which often wins others to their cause. Their courage
    and perseverance in the face of evil often wins them the victory, where warriors
    of less firm conviction fail.
  - Rangers tend to be loners, solitary heroes schooled in woodcraft and natural
    lore. Experts in stealth and tracking, in the wilds they are deadly foes.
  - Shepherds are drawn from fiercely independent rural peoples. Often forced to
    fight wild animals and hostile neighbors to defend their flocks, their simplicity
    and humility can be deceptive. They vary widely in their abilities - some are
    skilled in folk magic, others in combat, still others in stealth and woodcraft.
  skillDescriptions:
  - Your general fighting ability. This skill provides a bonus to your chance to
    hit when attacking.
  - Your ability to defend yourself in combat. This skill provides a penalty to foes
    who are trying to strike you.
  - Training in unarmed combat. This skill provides a bonus both to your chance to
    hit and to damage when attacking with only your fist.
  - Training in swordsmanship. This skill increases your chance of defending against
    attack and provides a bonus to your chance to hit when striking with swords and
    daggers.
  - "Training in the use of axes. This skill increases your ability to de\xADfend
    against attack and provides a bonus to hit when attacking with any form of axe."
  - "Training in the use of blunt weapons. This skill increases your de\xADfense
    against attacks, and gives a bonus to hit when using a mace or cudgel."
  - Training in the use of missile weapons. This skill increases the damage you inflict
    in attacks using bows, crossbows, and slings.
  - Your ability to manipulate magical energy. This skill increases your maximum
    number of Mana points.
  - The ability to correctly identify an item. This skill improves the accuracy of
    the information gained by looking at an object.
  - The study of spells. This skill improves the likelihood of a spell being successfully
    cast.
  - The ability to disable a trap. This skill disarms traps you find.
  - Training which heightens your perceptions. This skill increases your chance of
    detecting hidden doors and traps.
  - The ability to perceive animal tracks. This skill tells you when creatures are
    near.
  - The ability to move quietly. This skill automatically reduces the noise you make,
    making it less likely that creatures will notice you.
  - The ability to fix weapons and armor. This skill increases your chance of using
    an anvil to repair items successfully.
  - Knack of making friends. This skill increases your chances of obtaining a good
    deal when bartering.
  - The ability to use lock-picking tools. This skill increases your chances of using
    a lockpick to open a locked door or chest.
  - The ability to move with grace. This skill reduces damage taken from falls and
    collisions.
  - Training in perceiving the value of goods. This skill aids you in correctly evaluating
    a deal offered you in barter.
  - Training in endurance swimming. This skill postpones drowning.
  skillGoverningStat: 0100000001000000010000000100000001000000010000000100000002000000020000000200000003000000030000000300000003000000030000000300000003000000030000000300000003000000
